# Down to the Sea: a paper boat's journey, from a stream in the hills to the open sea. A showcase of the water features (docs/VIDEO_GENERATION.md, "Cartoons on the water"):
# rings and wakes, a river with rocks and rapids that carries things (`adrift`, followed by the shots), reeds, lilies and willows, ducks and a heron, a stone bridge, a watermill, boats
# and a lighthouse. Change the river's waypoints and the rest of the film goes with it; only the places by the bank are written down by hand.
film    down-to-the-sea
name    Down to the Sea
about   Pip sets a paper boat on a stream and it sets off by itself: through rapids, past ducks and a heron, under a bridge, round a mill, and out to the sea.
scene   film_assets/wild/set.pbrt
length  72
still   40
tags    water, river, sea, cartoon, showcase

terrain  coast  size 300  height 12  seed 2
water    sea  level 0  waves 0.22  wind 30  ripples 0.7
sky      16:20 17:50  south 60
exposure auto

